# Illusionary Mask's "could be paid by some amount of, or all of, the mana you spent on {X}" pays each symbol of the card's mana
# cost as a payment would, with mana only (the ruling: {U}{U} pays {W/U}{W/U}). With {U}{U}{U}{U} spent on X, Wildgrowth Archaic's
# {2/G}{2/G} could be paid, each monocolored hybrid symbol with {2} (CR 107.4e), and is cast face down. On turn 3, with {U}{U}
# spent, Fatehold Chronologist's {1}{W/U} could be paid, its hybrid symbol with its blue half (CR 107.4e); never Vault Skirge's
# {1}{B/P}, whose Phyrexian symbol mana pays only with black - mana is spent, no life (CR 107.4f).

